sequenceDiagram
  participant P0 as Laptop 192.168.1.10
  participant P1 as DNS resolver 8.8.8.8
  participant P2 as Web server 203.0.113.10
  P0->>P1: 1. DNS: Standard query A www.example.com
  P1->>P0: 2. DNS: Standard query response A 203.0.113.10
  P0->>P2: 3. TCP: 52411 → 443 [SYN] Seq=0
  P2->>P0: 4. TCP: 443 → 52411 [SYN, ACK] Seq=0 Ack=1
  P0->>P2: 5. TCP: 52411 → 443 [ACK] Seq=1 Ack=1
  P0->>P2: 6. TLSv1.3: Client Hello (SNI=www.example.com), 2 segments
  P2->>P0: 7. TLSv1.3: Server Hello + encrypted handshake, 3 segments
  P0->>P2: 8. TLSv1.3: Change Cipher Spec, Finished (encrypted)
  P0->>P2: 9. TLSv1.3: Application Data (HTTP request)
  P2->>P0: 10. TLSv1.3: New Session Ticket ×2 (encrypted)
  P2->>P0: 11. TLSv1.3: Application Data (HTTP response), 9 segments
